        "severity": "critical",
        "notes": "verdict: REJECT (proof invalid as written). referee_argument: The proof's final step (md:51-66) commits a category error: it derives m(ϱ) = ‖MI∫τ̂α‖ + ‖MI∫(α−τ̂α)‖ — a SUM of norms — from a PRODUCT of two SU_q(2) group elements, justifying it by 'submultiplicativity ... which is an equality'. Submultiplicativity gives ‖ab‖ ≤ ‖a‖·‖b‖; no norm yields ‖ab‖ = ‖a‖ + ‖b‖. Compounding this, the upstream factorisation MI∫α = MI∫τ̂α · MI∫(α−τ̂α) mis-attributes Yekutieli 2015 Prop 5.3 (the area-ordered multiplicative integral does not factor along an algebraic *-eigenspace split). The Pythagorean ‖α‖² split (true, additive, pre-integration) is silently conflated with the multiplicative group structure (post-integration). The additive mass-budget conclusion the lemma needs is therefore unproven; the proof must be rewritten with a correct relation between the multiplicative integral and the descent decomposition."
